    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d325-a2">

                <pb facs="0763" n="667" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg667"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 935.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Von Eisendecher to Mr. Munenori.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokei</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-08-01"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 1,
                        1879</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your excellency’s note of the 31st ultimo, in which you make known to me your
                    position in the quarantine question, and in which you further formally protest
                    against my action in the case of the Hesperia. I shall not fail to lay before my
                    government a translation of the dispatch.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to renew to your excellency the assurance of my highest
                    consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed>VON EISENDECHER.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
